61" 13194139534182 17592186045417 true] [17592186413320 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413309 13194139534182 17592186045417 true] [17592186413320 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139534182 17592186045417 true] [17592186413320 1077 "field-1" 13194139534182 17592186045417 true] [17592186413320 1078 #edb/ref 17592186413309 13194139534182 17592186045417 true] [17592186413320 1079 #uuid "e59f45ed-d037-5bd6-940e-13f41f6c836c" 13194139534182 17592186045417 true] [17592186413321 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413319 13194139534182 17592186045417 true] [17592186413321 1069 "q-101322" 13194139534182 17592186045417 true] [17592186413321 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534182 17592186045417 true] [17592186413321 1071 "Find the horizontal asymptote of $y=f(x)$ where $f(x)=\\frac{9{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-x}{5{x}^{2}+3}.$" 13194139534182 17592186045417 true] [17592186413321 1072 #uuid "88ec9ee8-0b06-53f7-bc3c-92317b5059e7" 13194139534182 17592186045417 true] [17592186413321 1074 "The horizontal asymptote is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{2}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{9{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-x}{5{x}^{2}+3} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{9{x}^{3}}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}})}{(\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(9x+1-\\frac{1}{x})}{(5+\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(9x+1-0)}{(5+0)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(9x+1) \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe limit does not come out to a finite number. Therefore, there is no horizontal asymptote." 13194139534182 17592186045417 true] [17592186413322 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413320 13194139534182 17592186045417 true] [17592186413322 1069 "q-339615" 13194139534182 17592186045417 true] [17592186413322 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534182 17592186045417 true] [17592186413322 1071 "Evaluate the limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{-{x}^{7}+3}{{x}^{4}+6x+2}=$\n\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534182 17592186045417 true] [17592186413322 1072 #uuid "d8cdb7dd-976e-5b44-901a-f1aa1b8415b7" 13194139534182 17592186045417 true] [17592186413322 1074 "First, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{4}.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{-{x}^{7}+3}{{x}^{4}+6x+2} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{(\\frac{-{x}^{7}}{{x}^{4}}+\\frac{3}{{x}^{4}})}{(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{{x}^{4}}+\\frac{6x}{{x}^{4}}+\\frac{2}{{x}^{4}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{(-{x}^{3}+\\frac{3}{{x}^{4}})}{(1+\\frac{6}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{2}{{x}^{4}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\text{ }\\frac{-{x}^{3}+0}{1+0+0} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\,\\,-{x}^{3} \\\\  & =-\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534182 17592186045417 true] [17592186413323 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413317 13194139534182 17592186045417 true] [17592186413323 1069 "q-101320" 13194139534182 17592186045417 true] [17592186413323 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534182 17592186045417 true] [17592186413323 1071 "Find the horizontal asymptote of $y=f(x)$ where $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{4}+1}{{x}^{3}-1}.$" 13194139534182 17592186045417 true] [17592186413323 1072 #uuid "e2d47372-f9cb-5c02-86fd-148b7f1d18b1" 13194139534182 17592186045417 true] [17592186413323 1074 "The horizontal asymptote is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{3}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{x}^{4}+1}{{x}^{3}-1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})}{(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(x+\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})}{(1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(x+0)}{(1-0)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }x \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe limit does not come out to a finite number. Therefore, there is no horizontal asymptote." 13194139534182 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0051830d-55e5-5121-b11a-0d87da7f40fb" 17592186413301 "answer-0e733fa1-bbd0-5f83-a1a9-64ce04aed72b" 17592186413302 "answer-18f73f57-316e-5fb3-bc4a-e767aaf24db8" 17592186413303 "answer-20243682-29c5-5259-864f-3c811fbe7f7d" 17592186413304 "answer-30464325-d158-5e08-93a8-e607ad63b4a6" 17592186413305 "answer-4f14c146-ddb9-57bd-ad6f-3930420ac403" 17592186413306 "answer-521202c4-e823-5b6e-92ea-799e96ebcde5" 17592186413307 "answer-9123a10f-7315-5079-b272-8ae329eb3b75" 17592186413308 "answer-955a14ee-2d66-50bc-8de3-377077da9e48" 17592186413309 "answer-95bed720-0647-52ed-9834-06d42bf8de74" 17592186413310 "answer-a7b385fb-ca34-55cc-a656-aaa065330917" 17592186413311 "answer-b4ee551d-2ce2-5847-a076-aa2475baa979" 17592186413312 "answer-cad17541-13af-57a0-9141-29e20640a0ce" 17592186413313 "answer-cf5c50b9-a9ea-50a2-a08b-b1461f5b7bb9" 17592186413314 "answer-db92d19b-e030-57a9-b3fd-2d1169f5e7a8" 17592186413315 "answer-f405f918-ce19-52f9-9c3d-f68c97ea5cd2" 17592186413316 "answer-field-36e0c9a9-15c6-51ff-ac4a-304c0aa988be" 17592186413317 "answer-field-381810c0-51a5-5b82-b7b6-6ce8ed23d924" 17592186413318 "answer-field-e22bffa8-51cb-5c7c-a8dc-24d845160961" 17592186413319 "answer-field-e59f45ed-d037-5bd6-940e-13f41f6c836c" 17592186413320 "question-88ec9ee8-0b06-53f7-bc3c-92317b5059e7" 17592186413321 "question-d8cdb7dd-976e-5b44-901a-f1aa1b8415b7" 17592186413322 "question-e2d47372-f9cb-5c02-86fd-148b7f1d18b1" 17592186413323}}
